  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1235 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nAfter a chilly start to the weekend, below normal and cooler \ntemperatures this weekend will begin to gradually trend warmer and\ncloser to seasonal normals by mid next week. Winds are expected to\nbecome light and variable with skies remain clear Saturday night\ninto Sunday morning, providing a good setup for radiational \ncooling. This would cause overnight lows to fall into the mid 30s\nto lower 40s across most of the area. Low-lying areas and river \nvalleys may drop into the mid 30s, which could bring the potential\nfor a light frost being experience across these areas that see the\ncoldest temperatures. \n\nA steady warm up will continue into the end of next week as\nupper-level ridging redevelops across the areas mid to late next \nweek. High temperatures are expected to gradually rise into the \nmid 70s to mid 80s by mid week, and into the 80s by next Friday. \nDry conditions are forecast to continue through much of the work \nweek next week.",
